From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 04:37:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] null renderer: software vertex shaders 16 vertices at a time,
 each distinct vertex once

A draw's distinct vertices (an indexed mesh uses each several times) are shaded once each, 16
at a time, so vertex programs run wide and in native code; each one's window coordinates and
clip planes are worked out once for all its triangles. Vertex attributes are read in place when
their stream is one range of memory. Window coordinates are rounded without lround's call.

A fragment shader's colour write while some lanes have left earlier (none waiting) writes only
the lanes running it, in the interpreter and native code; native code also stores vertex
outputs (SetAttribute) for the lanes run.

